    "narrative": "Today\u2019s slate for Ghost Ride the WHIP presents a challenging landscape, with the majority of our offensive core sidelined by off-days. With **Corbin Carroll**, **Josh Naylor**, and **James Wood** all unavailable, our scoring ceiling is significantly muted. **Travis Bazzana** stands as our primary focal point in the lineup, though his efficiency score of 41.99 remains in the marginal tier. While he benefits from a favorable matchup against Kay, whose 4.51 xERA suggests a hittable profile, **Travis Bazzana** is hampered by the L/L platoon disadvantage and a suboptimal position in the seven-hole, which strictly limits his counting stat upside for today\u2019s 5x5 Roto requirements.\n\nThe optimizer\u2019s decision to keep **Travis Bazzana** as the lone representative was straightforward, as our depth chart\u2014including **Vinnie Pasquantino**, **Jose Caballero**, **Mickey Moniak**, **Giancarlo Stanton**, **Seiya Suzuki**, **Trevor Story**, **Brice Turang**, **Isaac Paredes**, **Gabriel Moreno**, **Max Muncy**, **Moises Ballesteros**, **Dalton Rushing**, **Cole Young**, **Griffin Conine**, and **Edwin Arroyo**\u2014is currently entirely inactive. We are effectively in a preservation mode to protect our remaining games-played caps. The most pressing risk remains the absence of our elite speed threats, as **Corbin Carroll** and **Brice Turang** are not available to provide the stolen base floor we prioritize. Given that **Tyler Soderstrom** remains on the IL, we are essentially forced to absorb a low-scoring day to ensure we have maximum flexibility for the final push of the season.",
